CORE
main.c
--unwind 4 --rounds 3 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-assertions --datarace
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
Each thread writes its own copy of `static __thread unsigned slot` through
`&slot`. The copies were initialised in the spawning thread, after its
spawn event, so each initialisation was a write concurrent with the new
thread's own accesses, and once `&slot` was taken (making the copy shared)
it was paired with them as a race. The initialisation is now recorded in
the new thread, as the copies of the locals already were. Written directly,
without taking the address, the program was already SUCCESSFUL.

Reported FAILED before the fix, SUCCESSFUL after. Reduced from
libvsync/arraylock (no-data-race), which the fix also corrects.

See `thread_local_through_pointer_race` (slot not thread-local) and
`thread_local_escaped_race` (a copy reached from another thread): both must
stay FAILED.
